WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.150
Good morning Hank; it's Monday!

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.870
Goedemorgen Hank; het is Maandag!

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.860
Hank, that amazing historic building behind
those Nerdfighters... is a post office.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.790
Hank, today's video comes to you in five parts.
By the way, I had to put the puff on vacation

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.160
because I'm getting ready for the very fancy
Venice Biennale. I also had to by a couple

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.160
suits. Nerdfighters, do you like this shirt/jacket
combo? Because if you do, I will wear it at

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.160
a party, but if you don't, I won't.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.050
Right, that wasn't part one, that was just
a preface. Part one: the unicorn.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.531
So over the last month of living in Amsterdam
I have repeatedly had to use Google Translate

00:00:29.531 --> 00:00:33.930
to translate documents from Dutch into English,
and even though it's not a perfect tool, ovbiously,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.220
you usually get a sense of what people mean
and so you're able to be at the right places

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.220
at the right time or whatever.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.220
So two nights ago I had dinner with my Dutch
translator Eli and some publishing people,

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.690
and in the document describing that dinner
it was just, you know, a list of who was going

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.010
to be there, and then the last sentence of
the paragraph was this, which Google translated:

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.360
"We do not know which of them will eat the
Unicorn." And I was like "This is going to

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.340
be some dinner," because basically Hank, there
are only three categories of dinners. There

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.200
are dinners where there will be no unicorns
served, dinners where you know who will eat

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.850
the unicorn, and then there are the dinners
where you don't find out who is eating the

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:05.850
unicorn until you get there.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.101
Anyway, Hank, when we got to the dinner I
immediately volunteered to eat the unicorn.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:13.400
I mean, first off I know that unicorn blood
is restorative, and secondly I hate unicorns

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.141
because the fact that their blood is restorative
is the reason that Voldemort was able to,

00:01:18.141 --> 00:01:21.370
you know, kill so many nice wizards. But it
turns out it wasn't on the menu; I ended up

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.659
having the sea bass, which was also very good.

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:28.220
Part two: Gus, illustrated by Suzanne Van
Leir. Hank, as I'm sure you recall, when the

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:32.619
Yeti was pregnant with Henry, Nerdfighteria
made me illustrations of my favorite out-of-print

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.790
picture book so that I could read "Gus is
a Bug" to Henry. But Suzanne went the extra

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:42.759
mile, turning her illustrations for "Gus is
a Bug" into an actual book that Henry loves!

00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:45.670
And by loves, I mean chews on. I just thought
that was amazing, Hank.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:50.280
Part three: spoilers. So you will notice that
when I was talking about the unicorn blood

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.810
I did not say which wizards Voldemort kills.
Hank, I've often said over the years that

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:58.630
I don't believe in spoilers, but, to borrow
a phrase from President Obama, my position

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:03.840
on spoilers is evolving. Specifically it has
evolved from not believing in them... to believing

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.840
in them.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.979
This positional evolution has happened because
my new book is quite spoilable, and I realized

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:13.209
that I don't want it spoiled for readers,
so like nine months in advance, I am going

00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:18.930
to begin asking you and Nerdfighteria: please
don't spoil the book. We will work hard to

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:25.109
create safe spoilery places, and then there
will be the big, unblemished, unspoiled world

00:02:25.109 --> 00:02:26.239
outside, yeah?

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:28.620
By the way, Hank, I've started saying that
because people say that here, yeah?

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.120
Part four: punishments. Hank, we still haven't
decided on punishments; we need to do that

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.079
this week... yeah?

00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:38.070
Part five: Tumblr. Hank, you and I have both
been fans of the Tumblr "Eff Yeah Nerdfighters"

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:41.309
-- link in the dooblydoo -- for many years,
but it wasn't until earlier this month that

00:02:41.309 --> 00:02:45.419
we both got Tumblrs. We got them on the same
day. It's very cute how we do things on the

00:02:45.419 --> 00:02:50.870
same day. It's almost as if we're brothers,
you know, who really l-lo-li-like each other.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.709
Hank, Tumblr seems to be the number one destination
to find Nerdfighter jokes and Looking for

00:02:54.709 --> 00:03:01.150
Alaska quotations and DFTBA tattoos and Nerdfightastic
Google investigations and Pizza John/Looking

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.189
for Alaska jokes and entire websites devoted
to Humpy Hank. Hank, the Yeti is very amused

00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:09.689
by Humpy Hanks, but when she saw the one where
you hump me, she said "It's gone too far".

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:13.020
Anyway Nerdfighters, if you're on Tumblr you
should definitely follow Eff Yeah Nerdfighters.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.099
You can also follow Hank; he's at edwardspoonhands,
which in my opinion is the most under appreciated

00:03:18.099 --> 00:03:19.099
Hank song.

00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:22.900
And in my continuing attempts to profit from
the bounty of the ocean, you can find me at

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.400
fishingboatproceeds.tumblr.com.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.629
Hank, don't forget to be awesome; you'll see
more from Bruges on Friday, but first, I'll

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:30.009
see you on Wednesday.

